{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command the children of Israel.</b> What is stated above? 'May YHWH appoint.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: While you command me concerning my children, command my children concerning me — a parable of a king's daughter who was departing from the world and was instructing her husband concerning her children, etc., as is in Sifrei." "<b>My offerings.</b> This is the blood." "<b>My food.</b> These are the emurim, as it says (Leviticus 3) ״וְהִקְטִירָם הַכֹּהֵן הַמִּזְבֵּחָה לֶחֶם אִשֶּׁה״ (Sifrei)." "<b>My fire-offerings.</b> Those given for the fires of My altar." "<b>You shall observe.</b> That kohanim, Levi'im, and Israelites stand over them — from here they learned and instituted ma'amadot (Ta'anit 26)." "<b>At its appointed season.</b> Every day is the appointed season of the daily offerings."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:09.442719735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}